{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgw7988qtWqnDYT7ybYcY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The paper is written and compiles, but the overview figure is still a placeholder and the packaged validators could not run here.\n\n`paper.tex`, `claims_grounding.json` and `figure_manifest.json` are in `/workspace/paper`. The compiled `paper.pdf` has 8 body pages with the last page about 94% full, then references and the Supplementary Information. The claims check passes with 17 claims, the evidence verifier reports 0 dangling links, and 26 distinct references are cited. `validate_figures.py` and `compile_latex.sh` need the orchestrator environment (the `src` module and `pdftotext`), so I compiled with `pdflatex` and `bibtex` directly.\n\n**The result:** The sealed final outcome was `qualified`, and the paper is framed around that. A cross-fitted recalibration added as a second control variate to PPI++ narrows the mean interval by 2.2% on average. Reductions by family run from 0.2% to 4.0%. Against PPI with λ=1 the narrowing is 6.8%, and against the labeled-only interval it is 30%. Pooled coverage is 0.934 and the lowest family is 0.91, below the nominal 0.95. The evaluator's tests did not reject nominal coverage.\n\n**Additions beyond the strategy memo:**\n- **Headroom analysis:** I derived the closed-form variance ceiling (`analysis/headroom.py`) and computed it on the pools and synthetic regimes.\n- **The ceiling does not explain all of the gain:** The observed narrowing exceeds the ceiling in four of five families. Plankton is the clearest case: both the label and the predictor are binary, so the ceiling is zero, yet the observed narrowing is 3.5%. The paper says the source of that excess was not isolated and lists untested candidate explanations.\n- **Census income:** Most of its predicted gain (0.0179 of 0.0213) comes from the [0,1] clip on the PPI++ weight, not from nonlinear recalibration. I confirmed the clip by reading the public ppi-python 0.2.3 source.\n- **Partition scores:** Because of the evaluator's episode ordering, each reset-seed partition holds 76 episodes of one family and 6 of each other. The spread across partitions is reported as rough, not as a confidence interval.\n\n**Still to do and caveats:**\n- **Overview figure:** `figures/overview_setting_and_method.png` is a placeholder for the orchestrator to render. It is registered as `generate-concept-figure`, and the build script will not overwrite it once `.concept_figure_complete` exists.\n- **References:** I retrieved eight more entries (debiased ML, active inference, calibration, datasets, semi-supervised) and merged them into `references.bib` and the provenance file. Six irrelevant entries in the original bib are uncited.\n- **No ablations or per-episode data:** No controlled ablations, per-episode widths, or baseline coverage exist, so mechanisms are stated as hypotheses. The Discussion lists the experiments that would test them.\n\nThe paper uses \"Anonymous authors\" for the double-blind venue, and the LLM Usage section is in the Supplementary Information."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_read_input_tokens":225039,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2938f847-5226-44ac-88d9-3502f088dfe2","uuid":"0b79161b-2430-4032-b320-96f6da1f747b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T12:02:37.902Z","request_id":"req_011Cgw795x83GQDUgdpwPd7V"}
